Subject: [PATCH 0001] gaudi2: guard local MIN/MAX macro definitions

Kernel 6.8 provides MIN() and MAX() in <linux/minmax.h>. The Gaudi2 HBM
bringup source defines its own MIN/MAX, which trips -Werror=macro-redefined
and fails the out-of-tree DKMS build on kernel 6.8 and newer. Guard the local
definitions with #ifndef so they yield to the kernel's definitions when
present and remain intact on older kernels that lack them.

Verified: rebuilds cleanly on Ubuntu 24.04 kernel 6.8.0-139-generic.
Applies to: habanalabs-dkms 1.19.0-561 (see ../../vendor/habanalabs/SOURCE).

--- a/drivers/accel/habanalabs/gaudi2/gaudi2_hbm_bringup.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/habanalabs/gaudi2/gaudi2_hbm_bringup.c
@@ -71,8 +71,12 @@
 #define PHY_RREG(addr) hbm_phy_read(hdev, dev, addr)
 #define PHY_WREG(addr, val) hbm_phy_write(hdev, dev, addr, val)
 #define CEIL(numerator, denominator) ((numerator + denominator - 1) / (denominator))
+#ifndef MIN
 #define MIN(a, b) ((a < b) ? a : b)
+#endif
+#ifndef MAX
 #define MAX(a, b) ((a > b) ? a : b)
+#endif

 #define phy_poll_timeout(hdev, hbm_dev, addr, val, cond, sleep_us, timeout_us) \
 ({ \
